The round 3 work list, and the outcome of each item:

1. Grandma: the sleeve left the outer edge of the base upper arm bare, so the skin showed at both
   shoulders in the flat front render and in the flat side render. FIX. The sleeve cap now sits on
   the base shoulder joint and keeps an 8 mm clearance in every direction, so the base arm never
   shows through the knit. The flat front render holds no skin pixel in the shoulder band outside
   the neck, and the flat side render holds none outside the face.
2. Grandma: the garment read as a puffy-shoulder buttoned dress with a pale panel, where the drawing
   shows a textured knit button-front cardigan, open at the front over a matching green knit top,
   with a hip-length hem and ribbed cuffs, over a longer fuller skirt. FIX. The cardigan hangs open
   from the collar to the waist, so the matching knit top shows between the two front panels, the
   shoulder line is smooth, the hem carries a ribbed band at the hip, the cuffs carry ribbed bands
   at the wrists, the buttons run down the right placket, and the knit top carries a ribbed round
   neck and a ribbed hem at the waist. The puff balls of round 2 are gone.
3. Grandma: the skirt was short and narrow against the drawing. FIX. The skirt reaches lower and
   flares wider below the hip, and it keeps the vertical folds.
4. Grandma: the hair reads, so the brief leaves it alone. The hair, the face layer, the cheeks, the
   studs, and the flats are unchanged. The drawing has no glasses, so no glasses are added, and the
   hands stay as the base builds them, because the base hand is a thin slab that carries no held
   item.

The three largest differences of each look round of this round:

1. The sleeve left the outer edge of the base upper arm bare, so the skin showed at both shoulders.
   The cardigan read as a buttoned dress with a pale panel at the neck. The shoulders read as two
   puffed balls.
2. The sleeve moved onto the base arm axis with an 8 mm clearance, so the skin no longer showed. The
   cardigan got a front opening with the knit top behind it. The puff balls went and the shoulder
   came from the sleeve cap alone. The knit top ended above the base waist, so the base skin showed
   under the opening.
3. The opening now ends at the knit top hem, so no skin shows under it, and the knit texture got
   weaker, so the hem edge reads straighter.

